    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Build. Break. Improve. Ship.</strong></li>\n<li>A coding challenge for developers who want to solve real problems, write better code, and compete with builders from across the community.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>About the Challenge</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Aven Coding Hackathon 2.0</strong> is an online coding competition where participants solve programming and problem-solving challenges under time constraints.</li>\n<li>This edition focuses on <strong>logic, algorithms, debugging, optimisation, and practical coding skills</strong>.</li>\n<li>Whether you're a student learning to code or an experienced developer, the challenge is about one thing:</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Can you solve the problem?</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Hosted on:</strong> Unstop</li>\n<li><strong>Date:</strong> 21 September 2026, 12:00 AM IST &ndash; 30 September 2026, 12:00 AM IST</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ready to compete? Register on Unstop and get ready to code.</p>\n<p><strong>Who Can Participate?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>College students</li>\n<li>Developers</li>\n<li>Programmers</li>\n<li>Computer Science students</li>\n<li>Data Science &amp; AI learners</li>\n<li>Coding enthusiasts</li>\n<li>Working professionals</li>\n<li>Individual participation only</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Challenge Format</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Mode:</strong> Online</li>\n<li><strong>Participation:</strong> Individual</li>\n<li><strong>Eligibility:</strong> Open to all</li>\n<li><strong>Platform:</strong> Unstop</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Problems May Cover</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Data Structures &amp; Algorithms</li>\n<li>Problem Solving</li>\n<li>Python / C++ / Java</li>\n<li>Debugging</li>\n<li>Optimisation</li>\n<li>Logic &amp; Computational Thinking</li>\n<li>Real-world programming scenarios</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes &amp; Rewards</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Top 3</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Aven Coding Hackathon 2.0 Winner Certificate</li>\n<li>Priority consideration for opportunities with Kartexa/Aven</li>\n<li>Career Finder Partner Account</li>\n<li>Career Finder Premium Report</li>\n<li>Featured recognition across Kartexa/Aven channels</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Top 10</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Certificate</li>\n<li>Career Finder Partner Account</li>\n<li>Premium Career Report</li>\n<li>Priority consideration for relevant future opportunities</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Participants</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants who complete the challenge can receive a <strong>digital certificate/badge</strong>, subject to the event's completion criteria.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Why Participate?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Build your coding profile.</em></li>\n<li>Test yourself against other developers, identify where you stand, and add a real coding challenge to your portfolio.</li>\n<li>The best performers won't just get a rank.</li>\n<li>They'll get noticed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each participant must register using their own Unstop account.</li>\n<li>Submissions must be the participant's own work.</li>\n<li>Plagiarism or copied solutions may lead to disqualification.</li>\n<li>Participants must follow Unstop's submission and participation guidelines.</li>\n<li>In case of a tie, ranking may be decided using submission time and/or platform evaluation criteria.</li>\n<li>The organiser reserves the right to verify submissions before declaring final winners.</li>\n</ul>",
